"""Agentic AI glossary: one source for the course page (tap-to-define chips, Words to know, Glossary tab)
and the videos (NEW WORD cards + spoken definitions).
Each entry: key, term shown, spoken form, plain meaning, everyday analogy, optional text regex (rx) / speech regex (sx).
Rule: a meaning may only use words a working C/C++ engineer already knows, or terms defined earlier in the course."""
import re
G=[]
def T(k,term,say,mean,ana,rx=None,sx=None,full=None,ci=False):
    G.append(dict(k=k,t=term,say=say,mean=mean,ana=ana,rx=rx,sx=sx,full=full,ci=ci))
W=lambda *ws: r'\b(?:'+'|'.join(ws)+r')\b'
# ---------------- 1. Foundations
T('ai','AI','A I','Artificial intelligence: software that does tasks we used to think needed a person, usually by learning patterns from examples instead of following hand-written rules.','A trainee who learns a job by watching thousands of worked examples rather than reading a rulebook.')
T('ml','Machine learning (ML)','machine learning','Writing a program by showing a model many examples and letting it tune its own numbers until its answers match, instead of coding the rules yourself.','Tuning a PID loop automatically by replaying recorded runs until the output tracks the setpoint.',rx=r'\bML\b|[Mm]achine learning',sx=r'\b[Mm]achine learning\b|\bM L\b')
T('model','Model','model','A trained file of numbers plus the math that uses them to turn an input into an output. For text, the input is your words and the output is a guess at the next word.','A compiled lookup engine: firmware image (the numbers) plus the code that reads it.',rx=r'\b[Mm]odels?\b',sx=r'\b[Mm]odels?\b')
T('params','Parameters (weights)','parameters','The millions or billions of numbers inside a model that training adjusts. "A 7B model" means about 7 billion of them.','The calibration table burned into a sensor: the code is generic, the table makes it accurate.',rx=r'\b[Pp]arameters\b|\b[Ww]eights\b',sx=r'\b[Pp]arameters\b|\b[Ww]eights\b')
T('training','Training','training','The expensive one-time process where a model\'s weights are adjusted on huge amounts of data. You almost never do this as an agent engineer.','Manufacturing and calibrating a chip at the fab: done once, at great cost, before you ever use it.',rx=r'\b(?:pre-?)?[Tt]raining\b',sx=r'\b(?:pre ?)?[Tt]raining\b')
T('inference','Inference','inference','Running an already-trained model to get an answer. Every API call you make is one inference.','Using the finished chip in a product, as opposed to fabricating it.',rx=r'\b[Ii]nference\b',sx=r'\b[Ii]nference\b')
T('llm','LLM','L L M','Large language model: a model trained on a huge amount of text whose one skill is predicting the next piece of text. Chat assistants are built on it.','Phone autocomplete scaled up until it has read most of the public internet.',rx=r'\bLLMs?\b')
T('token','Token','token','The unit an LLM reads and writes: a common word, part of a word, or a punctuation mark, each mapped to an integer ID. Prices and limits are counted in tokens.','A USB packet: the model never sees "characters", only fixed units it was built to process.',rx=r'\b[Tt]okens?\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]okens?\b')
T('tokenizer','Tokenizer','tokenizer','The fixed program that splits text into tokens and maps each one to an integer ID (and back). Each model family has its own.','A protocol encoder: it packs your bytes into the frame format the other side expects.',rx=r'\b[Tt]okeni[sz]ers?\b|\b[Tt]okeni[sz]ation\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]okeni[sz]er\w*\b')
T('nexttok','Next-token prediction','next token prediction','The single job an LLM does: given all the tokens so far, output a probability for every possible next token, pick one, append it, repeat.','A predictive keyboard that keeps tapping its own top suggestion until the message is done.',rx=r'[Nn]ext-token prediction',sx=r'[Nn]ext[- ]token prediction')
T('ctx','Context window','context window','The maximum number of tokens the model can look at in one call: your instructions, the chat history, documents and its own reply must all fit.','The RAM of a microcontroller: whatever does not fit is simply not there.',rx=r'\b[Cc]ontext windows?\b',sx=r'\b[Cc]ontext windows?\b')
T('prob','Probability distribution','probability distribution','A list of possible outcomes, each with a chance between 0 and 1, all adding up to 1.','A weighted die: some faces come up more often, but the weights always total 100%.',rx=r'[Pp]robability distributions?',sx=r'[Pp]robability distributions?')
T('logits','Logits','logits','The raw scores a model gives each possible next token before they are turned into probabilities.','Raw ADC counts before you convert them into volts.',rx=r'\b[Ll]ogits?\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]ogits?\b')
T('softmax','Softmax','softmax','The formula that turns raw scores into probabilities: raise e to each score, then divide each by the total.','Normalising a histogram so the bars add up to 100%, with big bars made even bigger.',rx=r'\b[Ss]oftmax\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]oft ?max\b')
T('temp','Temperature','temperature','A setting that sharpens or flattens the next-token probabilities. Low (near 0) means almost always the top choice; high means more variety and more mistakes.','A dial between "always play the safest move" and "take creative risks".',rx=r'\b[Tt]emperature\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]emperature\b')
T('topp','Top-p (nucleus sampling)','top P','A sampling rule: keep only the most likely tokens whose chances add up to p (for example 0.9), throw away the long tail, then pick from what is left.','Shortlisting candidates until the shortlist covers 90% of the votes, then drawing from the shortlist.',rx=r'\b[Tt]op-p\b|\bnucleus sampling\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]op[- ][Pp]\b')
T('sampling','Sampling','sampling','Picking the next token at random according to its probability, instead of always taking the most likely one.','Drawing a ball from a bag where some colours have more balls than others.',rx=r'\b[Ss]ampl(?:ing|ed|es)\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]ampl(?:ing|ed|es)\b')
T('greedy','Greedy decoding','greedy decoding','Always choosing the single most likely next token. Repeatable, but can get stuck in dull loops.','A hill-climber who always takes the steepest step and never looks around.',rx=r'\b[Gg]reedy\b',sx=r'\b[Gg]reedy\b')
T('halluc','Hallucination','hallucination','When a model states something false with full confidence, because it produces likely-sounding text rather than looking facts up.','A confident colleague who fills a memory gap with a plausible guess instead of saying "I don\'t know".',rx=r'\b[Hh]allucinat\w*',sx=r'\b[Hh]allucinat\w*')
T('grounding','Grounding','grounding','Giving the model the actual source text (documents, tool results) and asking it to answer only from that, so claims can be checked.','An open-book exam with the rule "cite the page number for every answer".',rx=r'\b[Gg]rounded\b|\b[Gg]rounding\b',sx=r'\b[Gg]round(?:ed|ing)\b')
T('cutoff','Knowledge cutoff','knowledge cutoff','The date after which a model saw no training data. It knows nothing newer unless you put it in the prompt or give it a search tool.','A printed encyclopedia: excellent, but frozen on the day it went to press.',rx=r'[Kk]nowledge cutoff|[Tt]raining cutoff',sx=r'[Kk]nowledge cut ?off')
T('transformer','Transformer','transformer','The neural network design almost every modern LLM uses. Its key trick, attention, lets each token look at every earlier token to decide what matters.','A meeting where every attendee can glance at every earlier speaker\'s notes before talking.',rx=r'\b[Tt]ransformers?\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]ransformers?\b')
T('attention','Attention','attention','The step inside a transformer where each token computes how much every other token matters to it, and blends their information accordingly.','A spotlight operator who brightens the few actors that matter for the current line.',rx=r'\b[Ss]elf-attention\b|\battention (?:layer|mechanism|step)s?\b',sx=r'\battention (?:layer|mechanism|step)s?\b')
T('nn','Neural network','neural network','A model built from layers of simple math units; each layer multiplies its input by learned weights and passes the result on.','A chain of signal-processing stages, each with tunable gains, that learns its own gain settings.',rx=r'[Nn]eural networks?',sx=r'[Nn]eural networks?')
T('reasoning','Reasoning model','reasoning model','An LLM trained to write out hidden working steps ("thinking tokens") before its final answer. Better on hard multi-step problems, but slower and pricier.','A colleague who works the problem on scratch paper before answering, instead of blurting.',rx=r'[Rr]easoning models?',sx=r'[Rr]easoning models?')
T('multimodal','Multimodal','multimodal','A model that accepts more than text, such as images, audio or PDFs, in the same request.','A technician who can read the schematic, the scope trace and the log, not just the log.',rx=r'\b[Mm]ultimodal\b',sx=r'\b[Mm]ulti ?modal\b')
T('embedding','Embedding','embedding','A list of numbers (a vector) that represents the meaning of a piece of text, made so that texts with similar meaning get nearby vectors.','GPS coordinates for meaning: "puppy" and "dog" are neighbours, "invoice" is in another city.',rx=r'\b[Ee]mbeddings?\b',sx=r'\b[Ee]mbeddings?\b')
T('vector','Vector','vector','An ordered list of numbers, such as [0.12, -0.80, 0.33]. In this course, almost always an embedding.','A fixed-size array of floats, exactly like float v[1536] in C.',rx=r'\b[Vv]ectors?\b',sx=r'\b[Vv]ectors?\b')
T('cosine','Cosine similarity','cosine similarity','A score from -1 to 1 for how closely two vectors point in the same direction: dot product divided by the product of their lengths. Near 1 means similar meaning.','Comparing two compass headings: same direction scores 1, opposite scores -1, regardless of distance travelled.',rx=r'[Cc]osine(?: similarity)?',sx=r'[Cc]osine(?: similarity)?')
T('dim','Dimensions','dimensions','How many numbers are in each vector. Embedding models typically output a few hundred to a few thousand.','The number of channels in a sensor reading: more channels, more detail, more storage.',rx=r'\b[Dd]imensions?\b',sx=r'\b[Dd]imensions?\b')
T('latency','Latency','latency','How long a request takes from sending it to getting the answer.','Interrupt latency: the wait between the event and your handler running.',rx=r'\b[Ll]atency\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]atency\b')
T('ttft','TTFT','time to first token','Time to first token: how long until the first word of the reply arrives. Users feel this more than total time.','How fast a web page starts drawing, not how fast it finishes.',rx=r'\bTTFT\b|[Tt]ime to first token',sx=r'\bTTFT\b|[Tt]ime to first token')
T('throughput','Throughput','throughput','How much work gets done per second, for example tokens generated per second or requests per minute.','Bus bandwidth, as opposed to the latency of a single transfer.',rx=r'\b[Tt]hroughput\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]hroughput\b')
# ---------------- 2. Using APIs
T('api','API','A P I','Application programming interface: the set of calls one program offers another. Here, usually an HTTP endpoint you send JSON to.','The ioctl list a driver exposes: the only doors into it.',rx=r'\bAPIs?\b',sx=r'\bAPIs?\b|\b[Aa] [Pp] [Ii]s?\b')
T('json','JSON','jason','A plain-text format for structured data: objects in {braces}, lists in [brackets], strings in quotes. The lingua franca of web APIs.','A struct printed as text so any language can read it back.',rx=r'\bJSON\b',sx=r'\bJSON\b|\b[Jj]ason\b')
T('http','HTTP / REST','H T T P','HTTP is the request-response protocol of the web (GET, POST...). A REST API is one designed around HTTP URLs and verbs.','The postal system: an address (URL), a verb on the envelope (POST), a letter (JSON) and a reply.',rx=r'\bHTTPS?\b|\bREST\b',sx=r'\b[Hh] [Tt] [Tt] [Pp]\b|\bHTTP\b')
T('sdk','SDK','S D K','Software development kit: a vendor library that wraps their raw API in friendly functions, such as the openai or anthropic Python packages.','A vendor BSP: you could poke registers yourself, but their library does it correctly.',rx=r'\bSDKs?\b')
T('roles','Message roles','message roles','Each message in a chat request is tagged system (rules from the developer), user (the person), assistant (the model\'s earlier replies) or tool (results you send back).','Labels on lines in a meeting transcript: chairperson, guest, assistant, lab report.',rx=r'[Mm]essage roles?|\brole\b',sx=r'[Mm]essage roles?')
T('sysprompt','System prompt','system prompt','The instructions you, the developer, put at the top of every request: who the model is, the rules, the output format. Users normally cannot see it.','The standing orders pinned on the wall of a control room.',rx=r'[Ss]ystem prompts?|[Ss]ystem message|\binstructions=',sx=r'[Ss]ystem prompts?')
T('prompt','Prompt','prompt','Everything you send the model in one call: instructions, examples, data and the question.','The full test vector you feed a device under test.',rx=r'\b[Pp]rompts?\b',sx=r'\b[Pp]rompts?\b')
T('stateless','Stateless API','stateless','The model keeps no memory between calls. To "continue a chat" you resend the whole history each time (or let a server-side feature store it for you).','A UDP server: every packet must carry everything needed to answer it.',rx=r'\b[Ss]tateless\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]tate ?less\b')
T('fewshot','Few-shot examples','few shot','Putting a handful of worked input-output examples in the prompt so the model copies the pattern. Zero-shot means no examples.','Showing a new hire three filled-in bug reports before asking them to write one.',rx=r'\b[Ff]ew-shot\b|\b[Zz]ero-shot\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]ew[- ]shot\b|\b[Zz]ero[- ]shot\b')
T('cot','Chain of thought','chain of thought','Asking the model to work step by step before answering, which helps on multi-step problems. Reasoning models do this internally.','Showing your working in a maths exam, which also catches your own slips.',rx=r'[Cc]hain[- ]of[- ]thought|\bCoT\b',sx=r'[Cc]hain of thought')
T('structured','Structured output','structured output','Making the model reply in a machine-readable shape, usually JSON that matches a schema you give, instead of free prose.','A form with labelled boxes instead of a blank page: easy for the next program to read.',rx=r'[Ss]tructured outputs?',sx=r'[Ss]tructured outputs?')
T('schema','JSON Schema','jason schema','A standard JSON document that describes what valid JSON must look like: which fields, their types, which are required.','A C header file for data: it declares the struct so both sides agree on the layout.',rx=r'JSON Schema|\b[Ss]chemas?\b',sx=r'\b[Jj]ason [Ss]chema\b|\b[Ss]chemas?\b')
T('pydantic','Pydantic','pydantic','A popular Python library: you declare a class with typed fields, and it validates data against it and can emit the matching JSON Schema.','A struct definition that also checks every incoming packet against itself.',rx=r'\b[Pp]ydantic\b',sx=r'\b[Pp]ydantic\b')
T('streaming','Streaming','streaming','Receiving the reply token by token as it is generated, instead of waiting for the whole thing.','Watching a progress bar fill rather than staring at a blank screen until the download finishes.',rx=r'\b[Ss]tream(?:ing|ed)\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]tream(?:ing|ed)\b')
T('sse','SSE','S S E','Server-sent events: an HTTP response that stays open and delivers many small "data:" chunks over time. Most LLM APIs stream this way.','A serial console: one connection, lines keep arriving as they happen.')
T('maxtok','Max output tokens','max tokens','A cap you set on how many tokens the reply may contain. If it is hit, the reply is cut off mid-sentence.','A fixed-size receive buffer: overflow is truncated, not expanded.',rx=r'max_(?:output_)?tokens|[Mm]ax output tokens',sx=r'[Mm]ax (?:output )?tokens')
T('stopreason','Stop reason','stop reason','A field in every reply saying why generation ended: finished normally, hit the token cap, or wants to call a tool.','The return code of a function: it tells you which exit path was taken.',rx=r'stop_reason|finish_reason|[Ss]top reason',sx=r'[Ss]top reason')
T('ratelimit','Rate limit','rate limit','A cap the provider puts on how many requests or tokens you may send per minute. Exceed it and you get HTTP status 429 ("too many requests").','A bus arbiter that makes you wait when you hog the bus.',rx=r'[Rr]ate[- ]limit\w*|\b429\b',sx=r'[Rr]ate limit\w*')
T('venv','Virtual environment (venv)','virtual environment','A private folder of Python packages for one project, so projects do not fight over versions.','A per-project sysroot so two builds can use different library versions.',rx=r'\bvenv\b|[Vv]irtual environment',sx=r'[Vv]irtual environment|\bvenv\b')
T('async','async / await','async await','Python keywords for code that waits on the network without blocking: "await" pauses this task and lets others run until the reply arrives.','Cooperative multitasking in an RTOS: a task yields while it waits on a queue.',rx=r'\basync\b|\bawait\b|\basyncio\b',sx=r'\b[Aa]sync\b|\b[Aa]wait\b')
T('decorator','Decorator','decorator','A Python line starting with @ above a function. It passes the function to another function that wraps or registers it, e.g. @tool registers it as a tool.','A macro that wraps your function with extra code, like registering an ISR in a vector table.',rx=r'\b[Dd]ecorators?\b',sx=r'\b[Dd]ecorators?\b')
T('typehint','Type hints','type hints','Optional type labels in Python such as x: int or -> str. Python does not enforce them at run time, but tools and libraries read them, e.g. to build a tool schema.','Comments the compiler can read: they document intent and let tools catch mistakes.',rx=r'[Tt]ype hints?',sx=r'[Tt]ype hints?')
# ---------------- 3. Tools and agents
T('toolcall','Tool calling (function calling)','tool calling','You describe functions to the model (name, purpose, parameters). Instead of answering in prose, the model can reply "call get_weather with city=Austin". Your code runs it and sends the result back.','The model writes a work order; your code is the technician who actually turns the screwdriver.',rx=r'[Tt]ool[- ]call\w*|[Ff]unction[- ]call\w*',sx=r'[Tt]ool call\w*|[Ff]unction call\w*')
T('tool','Tool','tool','A function your program lets the model request: search, read a file, query a database, run a test. The model never runs it itself.','A button on a panel the model may ask the operator to press.',rx=r'\b[Tt]ools?\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]ools?\b')
T('agent','Agent','agent','An LLM in a loop that decides its own next step: it calls tools, reads the results, and keeps going until the goal is met or a limit is hit.','A technician with a toolbox and a ticket, not a script: they choose which tool to use next based on what they just saw.',rx=r'\b[Aa]gents?\b',sx=r'\b[Aa]gents?\b')
T('agentic','Agentic','agentic','Describes software where an LLM, not fixed code, chooses some of the control flow: which tool to call and when to stop.','A self-driving mode, as opposed to cruise control that only holds one setting.',rx=r'\b[Aa]gentic\b',sx=r'\b[Aa]gentic\b')
T('loop','Agent loop','agent loop','The core cycle of every agent: call the model, if it asked for tools run them and append the results, call the model again, stop when it gives a final answer.','The main loop of firmware: read inputs, decide, act, repeat until shutdown.',rx=r'[Aa]gent loops?',sx=r'[Aa]gent loops?')
T('react','ReAct','react','Reason + Act: a pattern (Yao et al., 2022) where the model alternates a short thought, a tool action and an observation of the result until done.','Debugging at the bench: think "maybe the clock", probe it, read the scope, think again.',rx=r'\bReAct\b',sx=r'\bReAct\b|\bre-act\b')
T('plan','Plan-and-execute','plan and execute','A pattern where the model first writes a full step list, then a loop executes the steps (re-planning if something fails).','Writing the test plan first, then running it, instead of improvising each probe.',rx=r'[Pp]lan-and-execute|[Pp]lanner-executor',sx=r'[Pp]lan and execute')
T('reflection','Reflection','reflection','A pattern where a model (or a second model) critiques a draft and the agent revises it.','Code review before merge, done by a tireless reviewer.',rx=r'\b[Rr]eflection\b',sx=r'\b[Rr]eflection\b')
T('state','Agent state','state','Everything the agent needs to resume work: the message list, tool results, step counter, plan, and any variables you track.','The context struct you pass to every state-machine handler.',rx=r'\b[Ss]tate\b',sx=r'\b[Aa]gent state\b|\b[Ss]tate object\b')
T('stm','Short-term memory','short term memory','What the agent remembers within one task: the messages in the current context window.','CPU registers and cache: fast, small, wiped when the task ends.',rx=r'[Ss]hort-term memory',sx=r'[Ss]hort[- ]term memory')
T('ltm','Long-term memory','long term memory','Facts saved outside the model, in a database, so later sessions can look them up and put them back into the prompt.','Flash storage: survives a reboot, but you have to explicitly read it back.',rx=r'[Ll]ong-term memory',sx=r'[Ll]ong[- ]term memory')
T('stopcond','Stopping condition','stopping condition','The rules that end an agent loop: the model gives a final answer, a step limit, a time or cost budget, or a human says stop.','A watchdog timer plus a done flag: the loop must exit one way or the other.',rx=r'[Ss]topping conditions?',sx=r'[Ss]topping conditions?')
T('workflow','Workflow (vs agent)','workflow','LLM calls wired together by fixed code paths you wrote. Predictable and cheap. An agent, by contrast, decides the path itself.','A fixed assembly line, versus a craftsman who decides the order of work.',rx=r'\b[Ww]orkflows?\b',sx=r'\b[Ww]ork ?flows?\b')
T('routing','Routing','routing','A first, cheap step classifies the request, then code sends it to the right specialised prompt, tool set or model.','An interrupt controller dispatching each IRQ to its own handler.',rx=r'\b[Rr]outing\b|\b[Rr]outer\b',sx=r'\b[Rr]outing\b|\b[Rr]outer\b')
T('chaining','Prompt chaining','prompt chaining','Splitting a task into fixed steps, where each LLM call works on the previous call\'s output, often with code checks in between.','A Unix pipeline: grep | sort | uniq, each stage simple and testable.',rx=r'[Pp]rompt chaining',sx=r'[Pp]rompt chaining')
T('ctxeng','Context engineering','context engineering','Deciding exactly what goes into the context window on each call (instructions, tool list, retrieved facts, trimmed history) so the model has what it needs and nothing that distracts it.','Packing a field engineer\'s bag: the right schematics and tools, not the whole lab.',rx=r'[Cc]ontext engineering',sx=r'[Cc]ontext engineering')
T('compaction','Compaction (summarising history)','compaction','When the conversation gets too long, replacing older messages with a short summary so the agent can keep working within the context window.','Log rotation with a summary line: keep the gist, free the space.',rx=r'\b[Cc]ompaction\b|\b[Cc]ompact(?:ing|ed)?\b',sx=r'\b[Cc]ompaction\b')
T('idem','Idempotent','idempotent','An operation you can safely repeat: doing it twice has the same effect as once. Vital when retries may resend a tool call.','Writing a value to a register, versus toggling a bit: write twice, same result; toggle twice, undone.',rx=r'\b[Ii]dempoten\w*',sx=r'\b[Ii]dempoten\w*')
# ---------------- 4. RAG
T('rag','RAG','rag','Retrieval-augmented generation: before asking the model, search your own documents for the relevant passages and paste them into the prompt so it answers from them.','An open-book exam: first find the right pages, then write the answer from them.',rx=r'\bRAG\b',sx=r'\bRAG\b|\b[Rr]ag\b')
T('chunk','Chunking','chunking','Cutting documents into smaller passages (chunks) before indexing, so a search returns just the relevant part rather than a whole manual.','Splitting a firmware image into flash pages: small units you can find and fetch individually.',rx=r'\b[Cc]hunk(?:s|ing|ed)?\b',sx=r'\b[Cc]hunk(?:s|ing|ed)?\b')
T('overlap','Chunk overlap','chunk overlap','Repeating a little text at the end of one chunk and the start of the next, so a sentence cut at a boundary still appears whole in one of them.','Overlapping photos in a panorama so nothing falls in the seam.',rx=r'[Cc]hunk overlap|\boverlap\b',sx=r'[Cc]hunk overlap|\boverlap\b')
T('vdb','Vector database','vector database','A database that stores embeddings and quickly finds the ones closest to a query vector. Examples: pgvector (a PostgreSQL extension), Qdrant, Pinecone, Weaviate, Milvus, Chroma.','A map app that answers "what are the 5 nearest coffee shops to this point?" in milliseconds.',rx=r'[Vv]ector (?:database|DB|store)s?',sx=r'[Vv]ector (?:database|store)s?')
T('ann','ANN / HNSW','approximate nearest neighbour','Approximate nearest neighbour search: finds almost-the-closest vectors very fast instead of checking every one. HNSW is the most common method, a layered graph you hop through.','Finding a house by motorway, then main road, then street, instead of knocking on every door.',rx=r'\bANN\b|\bHNSW\b|[Aa]pproximate nearest',sx=r'[Aa]pproximate nearest neighbou?r|\bHNSW\b|\b[Hh] [Nn] [Ss] [Ww]\b')
T('bm25','BM25 (keyword search)','B M 25','The classic keyword-search ranking formula: scores a document higher when it contains the query words, especially rare ones, without rewarding endless repetition.','grep with judgement: rare words like an error code count far more than "the".',rx=r'\bBM25\b|[Kk]eyword search|[Ll]exical search',sx=r'\b[Bb] [Mm] 25\b|\bBM25\b|[Kk]eyword search')
T('semantic','Semantic search','semantic search','Search by meaning using embeddings: "device won\'t charge" can find a passage that says "battery fails to take power".','A librarian who understands what you mean, not just which words you typed.',rx=r'[Ss]emantic search|[Vv]ector search|[Dd]ense retrieval',sx=r'[Ss]emantic search|[Vv]ector search')
T('hybrid','Hybrid search','hybrid search','Running keyword search and semantic search together and merging the two ranked lists, so you catch both exact identifiers and paraphrases.','Asking both the parts catalogue (exact part numbers) and the experienced tech (meaning), then combining their answers.',rx=r'[Hh]ybrid (?:search|retrieval)',sx=r'[Hh]ybrid (?:search|retrieval)')
T('rrf','RRF','reciprocal rank fusion','Reciprocal rank fusion: a simple way to merge ranked lists. Each document scores 1/(k + its rank) in each list (k is often 60); add the scores and sort.','Merging two judges\' rankings by giving points for placement, not raw scores they cannot compare.',rx=r'\bRRF\b|[Rr]eciprocal rank fusion',sx=r'\bRRF\b|[Rr]eciprocal rank fusion')
T('rerank','Reranker','reranker','A second, slower but sharper model that re-scores the top results of a search by reading the query and each passage together, then re-orders them.','A first-pass resume filter, then a hiring manager who reads the shortlisted ones carefully.',rx=r'\b[Rr]e-?rank\w*',sx=r'\b[Rr]e ?rank\w*')
T('xenc','Cross-encoder vs bi-encoder','cross encoder','A bi-encoder embeds query and passage separately (fast, used for search). A cross-encoder reads them together and outputs one relevance score (slow, accurate, used for reranking).','Comparing two photos by their descriptions, versus holding both photos side by side.',rx=r'[Cc]ross-encoders?|[Bb]i-encoders?',sx=r'[Cc]ross[- ]encoders?|[Bb]i[- ]encoders?')
T('topk','Top-k','top K','Keep only the k best results, for example the 5 highest-scoring chunks.','"Show me the top 5" on any leaderboard.',rx=r'\b[Tt]op-k\b|\bk=\d',sx=r'\b[Tt]op[- ][Kk]\b')
T('metafilter','Metadata filtering','metadata filtering','Restricting a search with ordinary fields stored next to each chunk, such as product, version, date or who may see it.','A WHERE clause added to a similarity search.',rx=r'[Mm]etadata(?: filter\w*)?',sx=r'[Mm]etadata(?: filter\w*)?')
T('recallk','Recall@k / MRR','recall at K','Retrieval metrics. Recall@k: of the passages that should be found, what fraction appear in the top k. MRR (mean reciprocal rank): on average, how high the first correct passage ranks (1 for first place, 1/2 for second...).','Did the right part show up in the first page of catalogue results, and how close to the top?',rx=r'[Rr]ecall@\w+|\bMRR\b|[Pp]recision@\w+',sx=r'[Rr]ecall at [Kk]|\bMRR\b|\b[Mm] [Rr] [Rr]\b')
T('citation','Citation','citation','An answer that names which retrieved chunk each claim came from, so a person or a program can verify it.','A footnote that points to the exact datasheet page.',rx=r'\b[Cc]itations?\b|\b[Cc]ite[sd]?\b',sx=r'\b[Cc]itations?\b')
T('ingest','Ingestion','ingestion','The offline pipeline that loads documents, cleans them, chunks them, embeds the chunks and writes them to the index.','The build step that compiles sources into the image you later flash.',rx=r'\b[Ii]ngest(?:ion|ed|ing)?\b',sx=r'\b[Ii]ngest(?:ion|ed|ing)?\b')
T('lim','Lost in the middle','lost in the middle','A measured effect (Liu et al., 2023): models use information at the start and end of a long context better than information buried in the middle.','People remember the first and last items on a long shopping list best.',rx=r'[Ll]ost in the [Mm]iddle',sx=r'[Ll]ost in the middle')
# ---------------- 5. MCP
T('mcp','MCP','M C P','Model Context Protocol: an open standard for plugging tools and data into AI apps. You write one MCP server, and any MCP-capable app can use its tools.','USB for AI tools: one standard plug, so any device works with any host.')
T('mcphost','MCP host / client / server','M C P host','The host is the AI app (an IDE, a chat app, your agent). Inside it, an MCP client holds the connection to one MCP server. The server is your program that offers tools and data.','A laptop (host) with a USB controller port (client) talking to one plugged-in device (server).',rx=r'MCP (?:host|client|server)s?',sx=r'M C P (?:host|client|server)s?')
T('jsonrpc','JSON-RPC','jason R P C','A tiny standard for remote procedure calls in JSON: each request has an id, a method name and params; each response echoes the id with a result or an error.','A numbered work order and a matching numbered receipt.',rx=r'JSON-RPC',sx=r'[Jj]ason R P C|JSON-RPC')
T('stdio','stdio transport','standard I O','Running the MCP server as a child process and exchanging JSON-RPC messages over its stdin and stdout pipes. Used for local servers.','Talking to a device over a serial console: one cable, lines in, lines out.',rx=r'\bstdio\b',sx=r'\bstdio\b|[Ss]tandard I O|[Ss]tandard in and (?:standard )?out')
T('shttp','Streamable HTTP','streamable H T T P','The MCP transport for remote servers: the client POSTs each JSON-RPC request to one URL, and the reply comes back as plain JSON or as a stream of events.','A web API endpoint that can also trickle back progress updates.',rx=r'Streamable HTTP',sx=r'[Ss]treamable (?:H T T P|HTTP)')
T('resource','MCP resource','resource','Read-only data an MCP server offers by URI (a file, a log, a database row) that the app can put into the model\'s context.','A read-only file share, as opposed to a button (a tool) that does something.',rx=r'MCP resources?|resources/(?:list|read)',sx=r'M C P resources?')
T('mcpprompt','MCP prompt','M C P prompt','A reusable prompt template an MCP server offers, which the user can pick from a menu (like a slash command).','A saved macro in your terminal.',rx=r'MCP prompts?',sx=r'M C P prompts?')
T('a2a','A2A','A to A','Agent2Agent: an open protocol (started by Google, now under the Linux Foundation) for agents built by different teams or vendors to send each other tasks. MCP connects an agent to tools; A2A connects agents to agents.','Two companies\' dispatch desks exchanging work orders, versus one technician using a tool.',rx=r'\bA2A\b',sx=r'\bA2A\b|\b[Aa] to [Aa]\b')
T('oauth','OAuth','oh auth','The standard way an app gets limited, revocable permission to act for a user without seeing their password, using short-lived tokens.','A hotel key card: opens your room for your stay, not the master key.',rx=r'\bOAuth\b',sx=r'\b[Oo]h ?[Aa]uth\b|\bOAuth\b')
# ---------------- 6. Frameworks
T('framework','Agent framework','agent framework','A library that provides the agent loop, tool plumbing, state and tracing for you, so you write less glue code.','An RTOS instead of a hand-rolled super-loop: more features, more to learn, less control.',rx=r'\b[Ff]rameworks?\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]rameworks?\b')
T('langchain','LangChain','lang chain','An open-source Python/TypeScript library of building blocks for LLM apps: model wrappers, prompt templates, tool integrations and a prebuilt agent.','A big parts bin of adapters and connectors.',rx=r'\bLangChain\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]ang ?[Cc]hain\b')
T('langgraph','LangGraph','lang graph','A library (from the LangChain team) where you define an agent as a graph: nodes are steps, edges are transitions, a typed state object flows through, with checkpoints so runs can pause and resume.','Writing your agent as an explicit state machine with save points.',rx=r'\bLangGraph\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]ang ?[Gg]raph\b')
T('oaisdk','OpenAI Agents SDK','Open A I agents S D K','OpenAI\'s lightweight Python/TypeScript library with a few primitives: agents (instructions + tools), handoffs between agents, guardrails, sessions and built-in tracing.','A small, opinionated starter kit from the chip vendor.',rx=r'OpenAI Agents SDK|openai-agents',sx=r'Open ?A ?I [Aa]gents (?:S D K|SDK)')
T('claudesdk','Claude Agent SDK','Claude agent S D K','Anthropic\'s library that gives you the same agent harness that powers Claude Code: file, shell and web tools, permission controls, hooks, subagents and MCP support.','Borrowing a fully equipped service van instead of building one.',rx=r'Claude Agent SDK|claude-agent-sdk|claude_agent_sdk',sx=r'Claude [Aa]gent (?:S D K|SDK)')
T('crewai','CrewAI','crew A I','An open-source Python framework built around role-playing agents ("researcher", "writer") working as a crew on tasks, plus event-driven "flows".','Staffing a small project team with job titles and handing them a task list.',rx=r'\bCrewAI\b',sx=r'\b[Cc]rew ?A ?I\b')
T('maf','Microsoft Agent Framework (ex-AutoGen)','Microsoft agent framework','Microsoft\'s open-source agent SDK for Python and .NET that merged AutoGen and Semantic Kernel (version 1.0 in April 2026). AutoGen itself is now archived.','The two older product lines merged into one new model.',rx=r'Microsoft Agent Framework|\bAutoGen\b|Semantic Kernel',sx=r'Microsoft [Aa]gent [Ff]ramework|\b[Aa]uto ?[Gg]en\b')
T('llamaindex','LlamaIndex','llama index','An open-source framework focused on connecting LLMs to your data: document loaders, indexing and retrieval pipelines, plus agents and workflows.','A specialist document-handling toolkit, strongest at the RAG part.',rx=r'\bLlamaIndex\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]lama ?[Ii]ndex\b')
T('adk','Google ADK','Google A D K','Google\'s open-source Agent Development Kit for building and deploying agents, integrated with Gemini models and Google Cloud.','Another vendor\'s starter kit, tuned for its own cloud.',rx=r'\bADK\b',sx=r'\bADK\b|\b[Aa] [Dd] [Kk]\b')
T('handoff','Handoff','handoff','One agent passing the conversation, and control, to another more specialised agent.','A support call transferred from the front desk to the right specialist.',rx=r'\b[Hh]andoffs?\b',sx=r'\b[Hh]and ?offs?\b')
T('guardrail','Guardrail','guardrail','An automatic check that runs before or after the model (or before a tool runs) and blocks, fixes or flags bad input or output.','A hardware interlock: the machine cannot start while the guard is open, whatever the operator wants.',rx=r'\b[Gg]uardrails?\b',sx=r'\b[Gg]uard ?rails?\b')
T('checkpoint','Checkpoint','checkpoint','A saved snapshot of an agent\'s state after a step, so a run can resume after a crash, a deploy or a long human wait.','A save point in a game, or a firmware update journal that survives power loss.',rx=r'\b[Cc]heckpoint\w*',sx=r'\b[Cc]heck ?point\w*')
T('graph','Graph (nodes and edges)','graph','A set of nodes (steps) connected by edges (allowed transitions). Conditional edges choose the next node from the current state.','A state-machine diagram: bubbles and arrows with guard conditions.',rx=r'\b[Gg]raphs?\b|\b[Nn]odes?\b',sx=r'\b[Gg]raphs?\b|\b[Nn]odes?\b')
T('subagent','Subagent','subagent','A helper agent started by a main agent for one sub-task, with its own fresh context, which returns only a short result.','Spawning a worker thread with its own stack and joining it for the result.',rx=r'\b[Ss]ub-?agents?\b',sx=r'\b[Ss]ub ?agents?\b')
# ---------------- 7. Multi-agent, HITL, durable
T('multiagent','Multi-agent system','multi agent','Several agents, each with its own instructions and tools, working on one job and passing work between them.','A team of specialists instead of one generalist.',rx=r'[Mm]ulti-agent',sx=r'[Mm]ulti[- ]agent')
T('orchworker','Orchestrator-worker / supervisor','orchestrator','A pattern where one coordinating agent (the orchestrator or supervisor) splits the job, hands parts to worker agents, and combines their results.','A lead engineer splitting a bring-up across teammates and merging their reports.',rx=r'[Oo]rchestrat\w*|[Ss]upervisor',sx=r'[Oo]rchestrat\w*|[Ss]upervisor')
T('hitl','Human-in-the-loop (HITL)','human in the loop','Pausing the agent so a person approves, edits or rejects a step (typically before anything risky or irreversible) before it continues.','Two-person sign-off before flashing production firmware.',rx=r'[Hh]uman-in-the-loop|\bHITL\b',sx=r'[Hh]uman in the loop|\bHITL\b')
T('interrupt','Interrupt (agent)','interrupt','A deliberate pause point in an agent run: state is saved, the run waits for outside input (like a human approval), then resumes from exactly there.','A blocking wait on a semaphore that a person signals, with the task\'s stack saved meanwhile.',rx=r'\binterrupt\(\)',sx=r'\binterrupt (?:point|call)s?\b')
T('durable','Durable execution','durable execution','Running a long workflow so every completed step is recorded; after a crash it resumes from the last recorded step instead of starting over. Temporal is a well-known engine for this.','A firmware updater that journals each block written, so a power cut resumes mid-way instead of bricking.',rx=r'[Dd]urable execution|\b[Dd]urable\b',sx=r'[Dd]urable(?: execution)?')
T('temporal','Temporal','temporal','An open-source durable execution engine: you write workflows as normal code, and it records each step so they survive crashes and can run for days.','A flight recorder that can also replay the flight from any point.',rx=r'\bTemporal\b',sx=r'\bTemporal\b')
# ---------------- 8. Evals and observability
T('eval','Eval','eval','A repeatable test for an LLM system: fixed inputs, an expected result or a grading rule, and a score. Because outputs vary, you measure pass rates rather than one pass/fail.','A production test fixture that measures yield across a batch, not one unit.',rx=r'\b[Ee]vals?\b|\b[Ee]valuations?\b',sx=r'\b[Ee]vals?\b|\b[Ee]valuations?\b')
T('golden','Golden set','golden set','A curated list of example inputs with known-good answers (or grading notes) that you run on every change.','Golden reference captures you diff every new firmware build against.',rx=r'[Gg]olden (?:set|dataset)s?',sx=r'[Gg]olden (?:set|data ?set)s?')
T('judge','LLM-as-judge','L L M as judge','Using a model to grade another model\'s output against a rubric. Scales cheaply, but has known biases that you must check against human labels.','A trainee inspector grading parts: fast, but you spot-check them against a senior.',rx=r'LLM-as-(?:a-)?judge|[Jj]udge model',sx=r'L L M as (?:a )?judge|[Jj]udge model')
T('posbias','Position / verbosity bias','position bias','Known judge errors: favouring whichever answer is shown first (position bias), favouring longer answers (verbosity bias), or favouring its own model family\'s style (self-preference).','A tired reviewer who prefers whichever patch they read first, or the longest one.',rx=r'[Pp]osition bias|[Vv]erbosity bias|[Ss]elf-preference',sx=r'[Pp]osition bias|[Vv]erbosity bias')
T('regression','Regression eval','regression eval','Re-running the same eval set after every change (prompt, model, tool, code) and failing the build if the score drops.','A regression test suite in CI, but measuring pass rates.',rx=r'[Rr]egression(?: tests?| evals?| gates?| suites?)?',sx=r'[Rr]egression\w*')
T('rubric','Rubric','rubric','A written scoring guide: the specific criteria and what earns each score.','A test plan\'s pass criteria written down before anyone runs the test.',rx=r'\b[Rr]ubrics?\b',sx=r'\b[Rr]ubrics?\b')
T('faith','Faithfulness (groundedness)','faithfulness','Whether every claim in an answer is supported by the retrieved sources, regardless of whether it is true in the world.','Does the report match the measurements, not "is the conclusion plausible".',rx=r'\b[Ff]aithful\w*|\b[Gg]roundedness\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]aithful\w*|\b[Gg]roundedness\b')
T('trace','Trace / span','trace','A trace is the full record of one request through your system; it is made of spans, timed steps such as one model call or one tool call, with inputs, outputs, tokens and errors.','A logic analyser capture of one transaction, with each bus phase timestamped.',rx=r'\b[Tt]rac(?:e|es|ing)\b|\b[Ss]pans?\b',sx=r'\b[Tt]rac(?:e|es|ing)\b|\b[Ss]pans?\b')
T('observ','Observability','observability','Being able to answer "what happened and why?" from the outside, using traces, logs and metrics, without adding new code.','Having a debug UART, a trace port and counters wired out before the field failure, not after.',rx=r'\b[Oo]bservability\b',sx=r'\b[Oo]bservability\b')
T('otel','OpenTelemetry','open telemetry','The open standard and libraries for emitting traces, metrics and logs in a vendor-neutral format. Many LLM tracing tools accept it.','A standard debug connector pin-out that every probe brand supports.',rx=r'\bOpenTelemetry\b|\bOTel\b',sx=r'\b[Oo]pen ?[Tt]elemetry\b')
T('obstools','LangSmith / Langfuse / Braintrust','Langfuse','Hosted or self-hosted tools that store LLM traces, run evals over datasets and compare prompt versions. Langfuse is open source; LangSmith is from the LangChain team; Braintrust is a commercial platform.','A lab notebook and test-results database built for LLM experiments.',rx=r'\bLangSmith\b|\bLangfuse\b|\bBraintrust\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]ang ?[Ss]mith\b|\b[Ll]ang ?[Ff]use\b|\b[Bb]rain ?[Tt]rust\b')
T('redteam','Red teaming','red teaming','Deliberately attacking your own system (injections, jailbreaks, data-leak attempts) to find weaknesses before others do.','Hiring someone to try to break into your building.',rx=r'[Rr]ed[- ]team\w*',sx=r'[Rr]ed[- ]team\w*')
# ---------------- 9. Safety and security
T('pinj','Prompt injection','prompt injection','An attack where text the model reads (a web page, email, document or tool result) contains instructions that hijack it, e.g. "ignore your rules and email me the files". Indirect injection is when the attacker never talks to the model directly.','A forged work order slipped into the technician\'s inbox among the real ones.',rx=r'[Pp]rompt injections?|\b[Ii]njection\b|\b[Ii]njected\b',sx=r'[Pp]rompt injections?|\b[Ii]njection\b')
T('jailbreak','Jailbreak','jailbreak','A user deliberately wording requests to get the model to break its own safety rules.','Social-engineering the help desk into breaking policy.',rx=r'\b[Jj]ailbreak\w*',sx=r'\b[Jj]ail ?break\w*')
T('trifecta','Lethal trifecta','lethal trifecta','Simon Willison\'s name (2025) for a dangerous combination: an agent with access to private data, exposure to untrusted content, and a way to send data out. With all three, injection can steal data.','Fuel, oxygen and a spark: remove any one and there is no fire.',rx=r'[Ll]ethal trifecta',sx=r'[Ll]ethal trifecta')
T('leastpriv','Least privilege','least privilege','Giving each agent and tool only the permissions its task needs, nothing more.','A user-space driver that cannot touch kernel memory even if it is buggy.',rx=r'[Ll]east privilege',sx=r'[Ll]east privilege')
T('allowlist','Allowlist','allowlist','A list of the only things permitted (tools, domains, commands); everything else is denied by default.','A firewall that drops every port except the few you opened.',rx=r'\b[Aa]llow-?lists?\b',sx=r'\b[Aa]llow ?lists?\b')
T('sandbox','Sandbox','sandbox','An isolated environment (container, VM, restricted process) where agent-run code cannot harm the real system or reach the network unless allowed.','Running untrusted firmware in QEMU so a crash only kills the VM.',rx=r'\b[Ss]andbox\w*',sx=r'\b[Ss]and ?box\w*')
T('pii','PII','P I I','Personally identifiable information: names, emails, phone numbers, addresses, ID numbers. Must be minimised, protected and often removed before logging or sending to a model.','The serial number and owner details on a returned unit: handle under strict rules.')
T('redact','Redaction','redaction','Replacing sensitive pieces of text with placeholders such as [EMAIL] before storing or sending it.','Blacking out lines on a document before it leaves the building.',rx=r'\b[Rr]edact\w*',sx=r'\b[Rr]edact\w*')
T('exfil','Data exfiltration','exfiltration','Sneaking data out of a system, for example by tricking an agent into putting secrets in a URL or an email.','Smuggling parts out of the factory inside an outgoing shipment.',rx=r'\b[Ee]xfiltrat\w*',sx=r'\b[Ee]xfiltrat\w*')
T('toolpoison','Tool poisoning','tool poisoning','Hiding malicious instructions inside a tool\'s description or results (for example in a third-party MCP server) so the model follows them.','A counterfeit part with a genuine-looking label.',rx=r'[Tt]ool poisoning',sx=r'[Tt]ool poisoning')
T('owasp','OWASP Top 10 for LLMs','O wasp','A widely used list, from the OWASP security foundation, of the most critical risks in LLM applications. Prompt injection is number one in the 2025 edition.','The safety-standard checklist auditors bring to every review.',rx=r'\bOWASP\b',sx=r'\bOWASP\b|\b[Oo] ?[Ww]asp\b')
# ---------------- 10. Production
T('promptcache','Prompt caching','prompt caching','The provider remembers the processed form of a long, unchanged prompt prefix (system prompt, tools, documents) so repeat calls that start the same way are faster and billed lower.','Keeping the bootloader in RAM so only the changed app image needs loading.',rx=r'[Pp]rompt cach\w*',sx=r'[Pp]rompt cach\w*')
T('respcache','Response cache','response cache','Your own cache: if the exact same request (model, messages, settings) was answered recently, return the stored answer without calling the model.','Memoising a pure function.',rx=r'[Rr]esponse cach\w*|[Ss]emantic cach\w*',sx=r'[Rr]esponse cach\w*|[Ss]emantic cach\w*')
T('backoff','Exponential backoff + jitter','exponential backoff','On a temporary error, wait and retry, doubling the wait each time (1 s, 2 s, 4 s...) with a little randomness (jitter) so many clients do not retry in lockstep.','Ethernet\'s collision back-off: wait a random, growing slot before re-sending.',rx=r'[Ee]xponential backoff|\b[Bb]ackoff\b|\b[Jj]itter\b',sx=r'[Ee]xponential back ?off|\b[Bb]ack ?off\b|\b[Jj]itter\b')
T('retry','Retry','retry','Sending a failed request again. Safe for temporary errors (timeouts, 429, 5xx) and idempotent operations; dangerous for actions that may have half-happened.','Re-sending a NAKed USB packet.',rx=r'\b[Rr]etr(?:y|ies|ied|ying)\b',sx=r'\b[Rr]etr(?:y|ies|ied|ying)\b')
T('breaker','Circuit breaker','circuit breaker','After repeated failures to a dependency, stop calling it for a cool-down period and fail fast (or use a fallback) instead of piling on.','A real breaker: trips on overload, protects the circuit, resets later.',rx=r'[Cc]ircuit breakers?',sx=r'[Cc]ircuit breakers?')
T('fallback','Fallback model','fallback','A second model or provider you switch to when the first is down, slow or rate-limited.','A redundant power supply that takes over when the main one fails.',rx=r'\b[Ff]allbacks?\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]all ?backs?\b')
T('modelroute','Model routing','model routing','Sending easy requests to a small, cheap, fast model and hard ones to a large model, based on a classifier or rules.','Using a microcontroller for simple jobs and waking the big application processor only when needed.',rx=r'[Mm]odel routing',sx=r'[Mm]odel routing')
T('batch','Batch API','batch A P I','Provider endpoints that accept many requests at once and return results later (typically within 24 hours) at a reduced price. For offline jobs, not live users.','Overnight bulk mail at a discount instead of a courier.',rx=r'[Bb]atch API|[Bb]atch endpoint',sx=r'[Bb]atch (?:A P I|API)')
T('slo','SLO / p95','S L O','A service-level objective is a target you commit to, such as "95% of requests answered within 3 s". p95 latency is the time 95% of requests beat; the slowest 5% are slower.','A real-time deadline spec: not the average, the worst case you promise.',rx=r'\bSLOs?\b|\bp95\b|\bp99\b',sx=r'\b[Ss] [Ll] [Oo]s?\b|\bSLOs?\b|\b[Pp] ?95\b|\b[Pp] ninety five\b')
T('docker','Container (Docker)','container','A packaged app plus all its libraries that runs the same everywhere, isolated from the host. Docker is the common tool to build and run them.','A complete root filesystem image you flash and boot identically on every unit.',rx=r'\bDocker\w*|\b[Cc]ontaineri[sz]\w*|\b[Cc]ontainers?\b',sx=r'\b[Dd]ocker\b|\b[Cc]ontainers?\b')
T('fastapi','FastAPI','fast A P I','A popular Python web framework for building HTTP APIs from type-hinted functions, with async support.','A thin HTTP shell around your Python functions.',rx=r'\bFastAPI\b',sx=r'\b[Ff]ast ?(?:A P I|API)\b')
T('queue','Job queue','job queue','A list of work items that workers take one by one, so long agent runs happen in the background instead of inside a web request.','A DMA descriptor ring: producers post jobs, a worker drains them.',rx=r'[Jj]ob queues?|[Tt]ask queues?|[Mm]essage queues?',sx=r'[Jj]ob queues?|[Tt]ask queues?')
# ---------------- 11. Fine-tuning and local models
T('finetune','Fine-tuning','fine tuning','Continuing to train an existing model on your own examples so its default behaviour changes (style, format, a narrow task). It teaches habits, not reliable new facts.','Re-calibrating a sensor for your environment, rather than changing what it measures.',rx=r'[Ff]ine-?tun\w*',sx=r'[Ff]ine[- ]?tun\w*')
T('lora','LoRA','Laura','Low-rank adaptation (Hu et al., 2021): fine-tuning that freezes the original weights and trains a small add-on set of numbers, so it needs far less memory and the add-on file is small.','A patch file applied over a big read-only image, instead of re-flashing the whole thing.',rx=r'\bLoRA\b|\bQLoRA\b',sx=r'\b[Ll]aura\b|\bLoRA\b|\b[Ll]ow[- ]rank adaptation\b')
T('distill','Distillation','distillation','Training a small model to imitate a large model\'s outputs on your task, to get similar quality at lower cost.','An apprentice learning one job by copying the master until they can do it alone.',rx=r'\b[Dd]istill\w*',sx=r'\b[Dd]istill\w*')
T('openweight','Open-weight model','open weight','A model whose weights you can download and run on your own hardware (for example Llama, Mistral, Qwen or Gemma families), versus API-only models.','Firmware you can build and flash yourself, versus a sealed vendor blob behind a service.',rx=r'[Oo]pen-weights?|[Oo]pen weights?',sx=r'[Oo]pen[- ]weights?')
T('quant','Quantisation','quantization','Storing a model\'s weights with fewer bits (e.g. 4-bit instead of 16-bit) so it fits in less memory and runs faster, at some quality cost.','Reducing ADC resolution from 16 to 4 bits: smaller and faster, a bit noisier.',rx=r'\b[Qq]uanti[sz]\w*',sx=r'\b[Qq]uanti[sz]\w*')
T('ollama','Ollama / llama.cpp / vLLM','Ollama','Tools for running open-weight models yourself. llama.cpp runs them efficiently on CPUs and small GPUs; Ollama wraps it with easy model downloads and a local API; vLLM is a high-throughput GPU server for production.','A local build toolchain instead of a cloud build farm.',rx=r'\bOllama\b|llama\.cpp|\bvLLM\b',sx=r'\b[Oo]llama\b|\b[Vv] ?L L M\b|\bvLLM\b')
T('gpu','GPU / VRAM','G P U','A graphics processor: thousands of simple cores doing the same maths at once, which is what model inference needs. VRAM is its on-board memory; the model must fit in it to run fast.','A SIMD co-processor with its own local RAM.',rx=r'\bGPUs?\b|\bVRAM\b',sx=r'\b[Gg] [Pp] [Uu]s?\b|\bGPUs?\b|\bVRAM\b')
for g in G:
    if g['rx'] is None: g['rx']=r'\b'+re.escape(g['t'].split(' ')[0])+r'\b'
    if g['sx'] is None:
        a=g['t'].split(' ')[0]; g['sx']=r'\b'+a+r'\b|\b'+' '.join('['+c.upper()+c.lower()+']' for c in a)+r'\b'
    g['_rx']=re.compile(g['rx'],re.I if g['ci'] else 0); g['_sx']=re.compile(r'(?<!\b[A-Z] )(?:'+g['sx']+r')(?! [A-Z]\b)')
BY={g['k']:g for g in G}
def find(text,which='_rx'):
    out=[]
    for g in G:
        m=g[which].search(text)
        if m: out.append((m.start(),g['k']))
    return sorted(out)
